  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Muncy broke a scoreless tie in the eighth. They still lost.",
    "what_this_means": "Gage Jump was better than a 1-2 final score deserved. He threw five scoreless innings with nine strikeouts on a night when the offense could barely find contact. The lineup managed three hits total and struck out seven times. Muncy gave them a go-ahead home run in the eighth, which should have been enough. It wasn't. Elvis Alvarado gave back two runs in the ninth before anyone could settle. The bullpen held everything else. Sterner, Harris, and Medina combined for three clean innings. But Alvarado's moment is what stays. This is a team that keeps handing away games it should win. Good pitching is no longer the floor. It's the opening act for inevitable failure.",
    "what_to_watch": "Landen Roupp held San Francisco to three earned runs last month, and Jeffrey Springs is bringing a 2.04 ERA to the ballpark tonight. Both teams know this is a pitching matchup. Which means whoever finds a run first wins it.",
